From: VLCDotNet CI <ci@vlcdotnet>
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: build libass with DirectWrite on desktop Windows

VLC's contrib only switches libass to the native DirectWrite font provider for
WinStore/UWP targets; regular desktop Win32 still pulls in `fontconfig`, which
in turn drags in `libxml2`. Both are fetched from the fragile
`freedesktop.org` / `download.gnome.org` hosts (and fall back to the now-dead
`downloads.videolan.org`). In one Windows run the arm64 job fetched
`fontconfig-2.12.3.tar.gz` from freedesktop.org while the x86_64 job -- hitting
the same host at the same moment -- was dropped and then timed out on the dead
VideoLAN fallback, failing the whole build.

libass 0.17.3 fully supports DirectWrite on desktop Windows too, so treat
`HAVE_WIN32` exactly like `HAVE_WINSTORE`: disable fontconfig and enable
DirectWrite. This removes fontconfig *and* libxml2 (the only remaining
libxml2 consumer once bluray/gettext are disabled) from the Windows contrib
closure, eliminating the two flakiest Windows downloads entirely. Linux, which
has no `HAVE_WIN32`, keeps fontconfig unchanged.
---
 contrib/src/ass/rules.mak | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/contrib/src/ass/rules.mak b/contrib/src/ass/rules.mak
index 4171273..3d65e50 100644
--- a/contrib/src/ass/rules.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/ass/rules.mak
@@ -20,7 +20,10 @@ else
 ifdef HAVE_DARWIN_OS
 WITH_FONTCONFIG = 0
 else
-ifdef HAVE_WINSTORE
+# Desktop Windows uses libass' native DirectWrite font provider (like UWP),
+# dropping the fontconfig + libxml2 contrib deps and their fragile
+# freedesktop.org / gnome.org downloads entirely.
+ifdef HAVE_WIN32
 WITH_FONTCONFIG = 0
 WITH_DWRITE = 1
 else
